From: bitbonsai <44185+bitbonsai@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Show real macOS caption controls during sidebar hover

Optional MA-007.c-caption candidate. Automated native regressions UNRUN.
Apply after corrected 0013 on Chromium
3e117efa80cec1c4e1e6fbfdf44edeb087a279a5 with
0002/0004/0005/corrected-0006/0007/0008/0009/0010/normalized-0011
and canonical 16-file foundation payload fd3880d.
0012 and 0014 are independent, not prerequisites.

Use the existing frame layout invalidated by region animation progress/end.
Real NSWindow standard buttons and layout reservation share caption bounds;
nonzero native hover width keeps captions visible through dismissal.
Remove the collapse-only writer that cannot observe temporary hover.
Limit ownership to normal in-process windows outside fullscreen.

Three production files, one native browser regression file. No VTSRegion,
BrowserView command/query, pin layout, model, page or lifecycle changes.
No added observer, timer, mock button or second animation framework.
Caption visibility snaps. AppKit translation, clipping and timing remain
unmeasured; this is not Arc motion parity or native acceptance.

See browser/experiments/native-hover-caption-controls.md and
browser/evidence/native-hover-caption-controls.json in myarc for exact
input/output hashes, patch order, checks and parent-owned runtime work.

